                        "review": "Wish I could love Armello again. Truth is I adore the game, its mechanics, and even didn't mind when they added the microtransaction shop. What has bitten me though, is that the servers simply don't work. To give you an idea, I've played almost exclusively multiplayer matches, and can confidently say after they added cross-play (this was a long time ago) I've only had a hand full of matches that didn't kick someone mid-way. Normally, this would be okay as whatever sure reconnect and we're good, but that isn't an option. Charging 25 for a game missing its beating heart feels like a crime.\n\nIf you get lucky, and the game works well, and the server gods smile upon you, its a delightful game I could easily recommend. Otherwise, you'll be frantically trying over and over to just complete a single match with your friends. The devs have openly abandoned the game citing \"We've done everything we can, but we don't have money left.\". I can believe the money ran out, but what I can't believe is that they've \"Tried everything\" when the game performs as it does online. Were it stable again I'd happily recommend Armello more as I have in the past, but as it stands it's dead in the water and a singleplayer experience.",
